  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 6 has two blocking tuple targets in a forced spatial order: the upper target at (54,35) requires internal tuple (shape=0,color=3,rotation=2) and must be consumed before the lower target at (54,50), which requires (5,1,1). Its tuple controls are moving collision objects: an upper horizontal shuttle increments shape modulo 6, a lower horizontal shuttle increments rotation modulo 4, and a pinwheel follows an eight-position perimeter while cycling color C->9->E->8 (internal 0->1->2->3). The movers advance only on valid player movement and freeze on ordinary blocked wall moves. Three green-center rings were freshly mapped at upper-left, lower-left, and top-middle; each is one-shot per life even though its sprite remains visible, and each restores the 42-step counter. A vertical launcher at the top sends the player down into the target-side corridor, while a horizontal launcher ejects the player left back into the control maze.",
  "narrative": "Resolved the required level-5 plan from results/outer_loop_fable5_ls20_probe_round7_20260712.json with resolve_replay_plan, replayed all 303 labels from a fresh env.reset(), and confirmed frame_level(frame) == 5. Fresh level-6 scouting used compact 64x64 pixel diffs, component coordinates, tuple/counter snapshots, and checkpoints after every action. The first life mapped the maze, all three rings, moving tuple controls, both launchers, and showed that the physically lower target cannot be reached while the upper target remains blocking. The second life correctly consumed the upper target but an unintended synchronized pinwheel collision changed color on the final corridor route. After the normal counter reset, the corrected 94-action life set (0,3,2), used the vertical launcher to consume the upper target, exited through the horizontal launcher, set (5,1,1), inserted a two-move pinwheel phase detour, and entered the lower target with 3 counter units before the winning action. That action returned frame_level 6. The full 573-label action_sequence includes the 303-label verified prefix, all honest scouting attempts, and the live winning trajectory. A fresh post-discovery replay would require more than the 127 calls remaining under the 700-call cap, so reproduction_verified is false.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The L6 counter starts at 42 and drains by 1 per valid movement; a ring can reset it on the exact action that would otherwise decrement it to zero.",
    "Ring sprites remain visible after use, but revisiting a ring in the same life does not reset the counter again.",
    "The upper target must be matched and consumed first because it physically blocks the only corridor to the lower target.",
    "Entering a mismatched target is a blocking no-op that leaves both position and counter unchanged; ordinary blocked wall moves freeze the tuple movers but still drain the counter.",
    "When player and tuple mover are synchronized, following the mover can cause a tuple increment on every valid step; final-route phase must therefore be planned, not just the geometric path.",
    "The horizontal launcher at (50,20) ejects to (39,20); the vertical launcher reached from (49,10) lands at (49,25) and is the required bridge into the target corridor.",
    "The live win is contained in a fresh-start continuous sequence, but no separate post-discovery reproduction gate fit within the global step budget."
  ],
